# NAME: Bybit Direct
# FORMAT: Surge RULE-SET (policy omitted)
# SOURCE: local gateway traffic observation, 2026-08-14 to 2026-08-18
# MIRROR: Graham-lo/surge
# UPDATED: 2026-09-03
# NOTE: Bybit endpoints that must bypass the proxy. ws2.bybit.biz resolves to Tencent
# Cloud and measured 17-21 ms direct against 85-99 ms through any proxy, the
# largest single saving in this profile. The spdtest hosts are the client's own
# route probes and must see the direct network to choose correctly. Reference
# this set with the DIRECT policy immediately before Bybit.list.
#
# Only list the hosts that are actually carried by a China-reachable acceleration
# network. Membership is per-FQDN on purpose: within the same apex, api3.bybit.biz
# is Tencent EdgeOne while api/api1/api2/api4/api5/ws/ws1/ws3.bybit.biz are Akamai
# or CloudFront and are slower direct, so a DOMAIN-SUFFIX rule here would be wrong.

# Market data.
DOMAIN,ws2.bybit.biz

# Account and asset APIs. These carry the transfer / deposit / withdrawal pages.
# Measured 2026-09-03 from the gateway, HTTPS to /v5/market/time, direct against
# the Bybit policy group:
#   api3.bybit.biz   Tencent EdgeOne (AS139341)   16 ms   vs  TLS 147-205 ms, TTFB 225-309 ms
#   api3.ng-dex.com  Wangsu CDN (public.bybithk.whecloud.com)  53 ms  vs  TTFB 254-329 ms
# The proxy penalty is not node-specific: all seven candidate nodes measured
# 620-970 ms against 111-120 ms direct on api3.bybit.biz.
DOMAIN,api3.bybit.biz
DOMAIN,api3.ng-dex.com

# Client-side route probes.
DOMAIN,spdtest-akm.byd3c3.com
DOMAIN,spdtest-teo.bynbc.com
DOMAIN,spdtest-ws.ng-dex.com
DOMAIN,spdtest-cft.ng-dex.com

# Domestic acceleration addresses.
IP-CIDR,43.135.121.179/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,43.154.61.67/32,no-resolve
IP-CIDR,43.160.158.108/32,no-resolve
